1bit OS, Lemonade Server appliance
Lemonade Server by AMD, running on the 1bit engine

The console is root, on this machine. What is here, and what to run:

  1bit-release-check              PASS/FAIL for this boot (mode, kernel, Secure Boot, GPU, NPU,
                                  Lemonade with its key, the catalog entries, a chat, the licences)
  1bit-selftest                   the engine answers, and where it ran
  lemonade list                   the models; models go in /data/models
  journalctl -u 1bit-lemonade -f  Lemonade's log
  apt update && apt upgrade       update from 1bit.gg/apt (signed repository)

The models, Lemonade's backends and configuration, and the SSH keys live on the 1BIT-DATA
partition, mounted at /data: they survive an update, a reinstall of the system does not touch them.
